-- ownership: calls in slice 1 (`ownership-checker.md` §6.1). With no
-- summaries, a call's result is a fresh list plus every argument list its
-- type could hold. `List.filter xs p : List Int` may be `xs` itself — the
-- identity promise of thesis §3.8 falls out of the rule — so extending it
-- while `xs` is read later is rejected, `call`, as the full checker would
-- (T52's shape). `List.map xs String.fromInt : List String` cannot be `xs`,
-- a `List Int`: the extension is accepted, `call`, pending the callee's
-- summary. `List.length` returns an `Int`, which crosses and holds nothing.
-- `[ …xs, …List.reverse xs ]` reads a temporary that may be `xs` while
-- writing `xs`: Disjoint fails only through the call, so it is rejected as
-- `call` (thesis §8.4: the identity promise is an approximate tag).
pub filtered : List Int → Int
filtered xs =
    kept = List.filter xs λx → x > 0
    grown = [ …kept, 0 ]
    List.length grown + List.length xs


pub mapped : List Int → Int
mapped xs =
    labels = List.map xs String.fromInt
    grown = [ …labels, "end" ]
    List.length grown + List.length xs


pub counted : List Int → List Int
counted xs =
    n = List.length xs
    [ …xs, n ]


pub mirrored : List Int → List Int
mirrored xs = [ …xs, …List.reverse xs ]
